{{Way_It_Works
| title  = How the Neural Firewall protects the mesh in four layers
| step1_label = Layer 1 — authenticate every transmission
| step1_text  = Every [[PsiLink]] node holds a cryptographic identity (private key + cert chain rooted in the mesh's trust anchor). Every transmission is signed at the source and verified at the destination. Signals failing authentication are discarded silently — spoofed packets never reach higher-layer processing. This blocks man-in-the-middle, injection, and replay attacks at the mesh layer.
| step2_label = Layer 2 — filter out jammer noise
| step2_text  = Continuously characterise the ambient noise environment by sampling between transmissions. Build a real-time estimate N̂(t) of the [[Psi Jammer]] noise profile. Subtract: Ŝ(t) = R(t) − N̂(t), where R(t) is the received composite signal. The cleaned signal Ŝ(t) feeds Layer 1's authentication check. Adaptive: filter coefficients update as the jammer's spectrum changes.
| step3_label = Layer 3 — isolate compromised nodes
| step3_text  = If a node starts emitting signals that fail authentication OR exhibits anomalous timing/pattern signatures (heuristic indicators of [[Neural Scrambler]] capture), the firewall flags it. Mesh-wide policy: isolate the suspect node, route around it, alert operator. Analogous to network segmentation that contains a compromised endpoint without disrupting the rest of the network.
| step4_label = Layer 4 — harden the hardware
| step4_text  = The underlying [[Neural Network Hardware]] is physically protected: TEMPEST-class shielding to prevent emanation-based attacks; EMP hardening to survive [[EMP Pulse Blaster]] hits; tamper-evident enclosures; redundant power. This is the substrate on which Layers 1–3 run — if the hardware is compromised at the physical level, the higher layers cannot defend it. Hardening makes physical compromise expensive enough to deter most attackers.
| step5_label = Compose the layers
| step5_text  = An attacker must defeat ALL FOUR layers to penetrate. Defeat L4 (physical hardening) + L3 (isolation) + L2 (noise filtering) + L1 (authentication) is exponentially harder than defeating any single layer. The defense-in-depth principle: probability of total compromise = product of per-layer breach probabilities.
| step6_label = Integrate with the broader defense stack
| step6_text  = The Neural Firewall handles INFORMATION-level threats; field-level threats are handled by [[Defense Discs]] (incoming psionic energy intercept) and [[Psi Ward]] (area exclusion). [[Psi Defender]] coordinates the whole stack. The Neural Firewall reports compromise events upstream to [[PsiSys]] for situational awareness and threat-trend analysis.
}}

